  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Factorise $\\left(1+\\frac{y^2+z^2-x^2}{2yz}\\right)\\div\\left(1-\\frac{x^2+y^2-z^2}{2xy}\\right)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{x(x+y+z)}{z(x-y+z)}$\n\nCombine each bracket into one fraction, factorise the differences of squares, then multiply by the reciprocal and cancel.",
      "worked": "Let $E$ denote the given expression.\n$$\\begin{align*}E&=\\frac{2yz+y^2+z^2-x^2}{2yz}\\div\\frac{2xy-x^2-y^2+z^2}{2xy}\\\\E&=\\frac{(y+z)^2-x^2}{2yz}\\div\\frac{z^2-(x-y)^2}{2xy}\\\\E&=\\frac{(y+z-x)(y+z+x)}{2yz}\\times\\frac{2xy}{(z-x+y)(z+x-y)}\\\\E&=\\frac{x(x+y+z)}{z(x-y+z)}\\end{align*}$$\nHere $y+z-x=z-x+y$, so these common factors cancel. The original expression requires $x,y,z\\ne0$, $z-x+y\\ne0$ and $z+x-y\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
